description: v042 recipe EXACTLY, on the patched trainer, with training.state_reset=4000
  matching inference. Full 3 epochs. This is the run that prices the state-carry fix.
hypothesis: v042 scored full_valid_wp 0.688268 and public 0.6600 while training on
  1000 steps of context and being served on 4000. With the state actually carried,
  and the training horizon matched to the serving horizon, the same recipe should
  do something -- and the direction is the whole question. If it beats 0.688268 by
  more than the 0.0004 public seed noise, the bug was costing us real score and every
  closed axis (preprocessing, capacity, distill_weight, schedule) deserves re-testing
  on the fixed trainer. If it does not, then the model was not context-limited and
  the plateau is genuine.
change_vs_parent: the state-carry PATCH (state now carried across chunks with truncated
  BPTT), plus training.state_reset 2000 -> 4000 to match inference.state_reset. Full
  3 epochs, unlike the 1-epoch sweep runs v051/v052/v053.
